Throwing that Exceptions 
● Can throw a primitive as an exception 
try{ 
... 
throw 20; 
}catch(int e) { cout << “Error: ” << e << endl; } 
● Best way to catch your own exception: 
try{ 
throw MyException(); 
}catch(MyException & e) { 
cout << e.what() << endl; 
} 
